# Reference integrity: every entity IRI used as an object must resolve to a
# record that is itself described (has a type). A cross-reference to a ULID no
# record carries - a typo, a deleted record, a draft that never landed - leaves
# a dangling IRI: RDF does not care, the generated JSON Schema only checks the
# 26-character shape of the value, and no structural shape targets it, so
# nothing else in the pipeline notices.
#
# The subject side is deliberately unconstrained (`?s ?p ?ref`): a reference
# can be a predicate's object or the object of a nested relation, and the
# question is the same either way.
#
# Vacuity is guarded in the Makefile recipe (the export must mention entity
# IRIs) rather than here: an empty result is the PASS, so the query cannot
# distinguish "all references resolve" from "there was nothing to check".
PREFIX martialis: <https://w3id.org/martialis/ontology#>

SELECT DISTINCT ?ref
WHERE {
  ?s ?p ?ref .
  FILTER(isIRI(?ref))
  FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?ref), "https://martial.is/entity/"))
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?ref a ?type }
}
ORDER BY ?ref
